error: `ready` holds the thread until it is done, and an async function does not hold its thread
  `ready` calls `File.exists`, which waits for the disk
  the tasks of async functions share a few threads: one that holds its thread keeps the others from running
  --> error_async_file_exists_inner.sg:8:11
 8 |     print(ready("a.txt"))
   |           ^^^^^
  hint: a function that does it runs on a thread of its own with `await Task.run(work, x)`
